WEBVTT

00:01.400 --> 00:04.914
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.915 --> 00:08.184
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.185 --> 00:11.889
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.890 --> 00:14.858
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.859 --> 00:18.308
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.309 --> 00:21.588
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:21.589 --> 00:23.296
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.297 --> 00:24.835
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.836 --> 00:30.409
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:36.091 --> 00:38.149
Stone fruit season!

00:38.150 --> 00:40.618
Now, those are what my granddaddy called

00:40.619 --> 00:42.253
"proposin' peaches."

00:42.254 --> 00:44.188
Don't be shy, now. Dig in.

00:49.260 --> 00:51.363
Whoa-ho!

00:52.979 --> 00:54.865
Here I go.

00:59.403 --> 01:02.165
Don't you do it.
Don't you go to the gross side.

01:02.166 --> 01:03.707
It's out of my control.

01:03.708 --> 01:05.208
They're too... juicy.

01:05.209 --> 01:06.844
We exchanged a look earlier.

01:06.845 --> 01:09.213
We have a grossed-out, no-fun alliance.

01:10.682 --> 01:12.683
So, you guys like peaches, huh?

01:12.684 --> 01:13.984
- Yeah.
- Hold on.

01:13.985 --> 01:16.087
I need a large pane of glass.

01:17.087 --> 01:19.089
Well, I got her phone number.

01:19.090 --> 01:21.058
<i>How do you like them peaches?</i>

01:22.727 --> 01:24.961
Covered by most insurance.

01:24.962 --> 01:27.064
Guys, check it out.

01:27.065 --> 01:29.767
<i>In honor of opening day
at Fenway Park this weekend,</i>

01:29.768 --> 01:32.869
<i>the Red Sox are offering
four tickets behind home plate</i>

01:32.870 --> 01:35.599
<i>to the person who makes
the best Red Sox ad.</i>

01:35.600 --> 01:37.508
- Oh...
- My...

01:37.509 --> 01:40.344
Freaking...

01:40.345 --> 01:43.246
Guys, winning those seats
is our highest priority.

01:43.247 --> 01:46.391
Even higher than my dream
of winning socks-on karate.

01:51.388 --> 01:53.090
Point! Winner!

01:53.091 --> 01:54.627
- Ow!
- Ow!

02:00.097 --> 02:01.764
Ah, this is the life.

02:01.765 --> 02:04.535
- Thanks, Peter.
- I still can't believe you won

02:04.536 --> 02:06.870
by filming yourself pooping
in a Yankees helmet.

02:06.871 --> 02:08.805
I am not a subtle filmmaker,

02:08.806 --> 02:11.275
and my audience
wouldn't have it any other way.

02:11.276 --> 02:14.043
Joe, what are you eating
your ice cream out of?

02:14.044 --> 02:16.447
They ran out of those
mini batting helmets,

02:16.448 --> 02:18.582
so they're serving it in athletic cups.

02:18.583 --> 02:20.618
Did you buy that
from a certified vendor?

02:20.619 --> 02:23.787
He wasn't behind the counter,
but he had a blue shirt on.

02:23.788 --> 02:26.590
I think somebody might be
having a little fun with you.

02:26.591 --> 02:29.425
Yeah, come to think of it,
he did have a friend filming,

02:29.426 --> 02:32.562
and he made me eat the first
seven bites in front of him,

02:32.563 --> 02:34.465
and he didn't charge me anything.

02:34.466 --> 02:36.000
Do you, uh...

02:36.001 --> 02:37.800
do you want this?

02:37.801 --> 02:40.003
I'll take a bite.

02:40.004 --> 02:42.007
Four beers, please.

02:43.407 --> 02:44.841
Anything else, fellas?

02:44.842 --> 02:46.644
Uh, yeah, I'll have a beer.

02:46.645 --> 02:48.078
Anyone else want another?

02:48.079 --> 02:49.613
Yeah, why not?

02:49.614 --> 02:51.215
- Quagmire?
- I'm good.

02:51.216 --> 02:53.250
I'm good with one more.

02:53.251 --> 02:54.518
- Cleveland?
- I'm fine.

02:54.519 --> 02:56.519
Yeah, I'm fine with one more, too.

02:56.520 --> 02:59.290
I-I'm gonna take it with me to the can.

03:05.729 --> 03:08.465
All right, now to have
the only exciting thing

03:08.466 --> 03:11.668
in the game happen
as soon as I turn my back.

03:40.497 --> 03:42.333
Hey, buddy,
that's just a break in the line

03:42.334 --> 03:43.701
so people can pass through.

03:43.702 --> 03:45.169
End of the line's that way.

03:46.905 --> 03:49.205
Yeah, it's all the way
to that guy with the scorebook

03:49.206 --> 03:50.907
just waiting for someone to talk to.

03:50.908 --> 03:52.942
Don't get used to Benintendi's
two-strike hitting.

03:52.943 --> 03:55.546
His history will tell you
it's not a sustainable pace

03:55.547 --> 03:57.080
for an everyday outfielder.

03:57.081 --> 03:59.083
Aw, screw that.
I'm using the ladies' room.

03:59.084 --> 04:00.518
How bad could it be?

04:02.987 --> 04:04.454
I saw a mouse.

04:04.455 --> 04:07.191
Buddy, if you really gotta go,
you can use that one.

04:09.227 --> 04:10.894
A bathroom for Prince?

04:10.895 --> 04:12.896
I can't use that. I'm not Prince.

04:12.897 --> 04:14.665
It's not for Prince.

04:14.666 --> 04:17.401
Space Cats? I'm not a Space Cat.

04:17.402 --> 04:21.005
Sir, I can assure you there's
no such thing as Space Cats.

04:21.006 --> 04:23.973
Now, can you direct me
to Earth's reserve of yarn?

04:23.974 --> 04:26.276
Aw, screw this.

04:26.277 --> 04:28.411
Excuse me, ma'am, could you direct me

04:28.412 --> 04:31.315
to Earth's reserve
of near-empty tuna tins?

04:31.316 --> 04:33.385
Are you a Space Cat?

04:35.052 --> 04:37.120
- He's been made.
- We've got to call him back.

04:38.123 --> 04:39.255
Psst, psst.

04:39.256 --> 04:40.925
Psst, psst.

04:43.260 --> 04:45.728
Guys! I found the best toilet
in the whole place.

04:45.729 --> 04:48.899
- Next time...
- Peter! You're on the jumbotron!

04:48.900 --> 04:50.901
- Where?
- Right there!

04:50.902 --> 04:52.903
- Here?
- There, Peter, there!

04:52.904 --> 04:54.038
Here? Yes?

04:54.039 --> 04:55.906
It's right in front of you, Peter!

04:55.907 --> 04:57.608
- Right here?
- No!

04:57.609 --> 04:59.142
- Oh, over here?
- Damn it, Peter,

04:59.143 --> 05:00.444
you're gonna miss it!

05:00.445 --> 05:02.178
Is-is this... is this it?

05:02.179 --> 05:04.380
Aha! Where?

05:04.381 --> 05:07.183
Guys, look! I'm on the jumbotron!

05:07.184 --> 05:09.219
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>

05:09.220 --> 05:11.622
<i>let's give a big Boston welcome
to Peter Griffin,</i>

05:11.623 --> 05:14.925
<i>the fist transgender Red Sox fan.</i>

05:14.926 --> 05:17.161
Peter, you used
the transgender bathroom,

05:17.162 --> 05:19.829
so now everyone thinks
you're transgender.

05:19.830 --> 05:22.199
Cleveland, what are you eating
your Cracker Jacks out of?

05:22.200 --> 05:24.668
Oh, the guy said they
were out of regular boxes,

05:24.669 --> 05:27.570
- so he gave me this box.
- What did he look like?

05:27.571 --> 05:28.872
Like this.

05:28.873 --> 05:31.608
Hey, that's the ice cream guy!

05:31.609 --> 05:33.644
I got a handful, too, Peter.

05:33.645 --> 05:35.846
You want to see who can finish faster?

05:35.847 --> 05:37.146
You're on!

05:37.147 --> 05:39.048
It looks like we've got ourselves

05:39.049 --> 05:41.486
a good old-fashioned Cracker Jack off.

05:47.025 --> 05:49.526
Good morning, Peter.
We saw the game last night,

05:49.527 --> 05:51.594
and, well, we just want you to know

05:51.595 --> 05:54.497
that we wholeheartedly support
all transgender people.

05:54.498 --> 05:56.834
- But I'm not...
- Peter, before you say anything

05:56.835 --> 05:59.469
that might clear all this up,
let me tell you

05:59.470 --> 06:03.372
about our stellar transgender
employee benefit package.

06:03.373 --> 06:05.743
Benefits? I'm trans-listening.

06:05.744 --> 06:08.879
Well, as such, you're entitled
to supplemental time off,

06:08.880 --> 06:10.413
our on-site masseuse

06:10.414 --> 06:13.016
and a $60 gift card from Nordstrom Rack.

06:13.017 --> 06:14.651
- Nordstrom?!
- Rack.

06:14.652 --> 06:16.653
- Yeah, but Nordstrom!
- Yes, I understand.

06:16.654 --> 06:18.221
But it's just... Rack.

06:18.222 --> 06:21.190
Well, in the words
of trailblazer Caitlyn Jenner,

06:21.191 --> 06:23.793
"I will do anything
for money and attention."

06:23.794 --> 06:25.228
So brave.

06:25.229 --> 06:28.565
Great. We'll send the paperwork
down to your office.

06:28.566 --> 06:31.300
Well, better use
the men's room one last time.

06:31.301 --> 06:33.403
Lot of history in there.

06:40.677 --> 06:41.846
You.

06:42.847 --> 06:45.481
And you, the Hungry Hungry Hippo.

06:45.482 --> 06:48.851
You'd always swallow it
before I could see what I did.

06:48.852 --> 06:52.523
And one last look at my crack
imprint on the walk of fame.

06:54.539 --> 06:56.709
God, I remember that day.

06:58.530 --> 07:00.029
<i>I would find out later</i>

07:00.030 --> 07:02.332
<i>that when you put your ass
in wet cement,</i>

07:02.333 --> 07:03.933
<i>you're just sealing it shut forever.</i>

07:03.934 --> 07:06.235
<i>Best they could do was poke holes in it</i>

07:06.236 --> 07:08.639
<i>so it comes out like Play-Doh spaghetti.</i>

07:08.640 --> 07:11.376
<i>Anyway, that's the first act.</i>

07:16.614 --> 07:19.716
Peter, pretending to be
transgender to get time off work

07:19.717 --> 07:22.618
trivializes a real struggle
in this country.

07:22.619 --> 07:25.154
Did the... did the Space Cats
get to you?

07:25.155 --> 07:28.625
I don't know what that is,
but you got to knock this off.

07:28.626 --> 07:32.495
And direct me to Earth's reserve
of sun-dappled window seats.

07:32.496 --> 07:33.896
Lois is right, Peter.

07:33.897 --> 07:36.132
Besides the fact that
you're lying to your employers,

07:36.133 --> 07:37.935
you're taking advantage
of a civil liberty

07:37.936 --> 07:39.336
that so many oppressed people

07:39.337 --> 07:40.803
have fought their entire lives for.

07:40.804 --> 07:43.272
Shut your mouth, Brian.
I'm part of a movement.

07:43.273 --> 07:44.641
Hey, what is "transgender," anyway?

07:44.642 --> 07:46.375
Is that the stuff in potato chips

07:46.376 --> 07:48.077
that makes your bum go bam?

07:48.078 --> 07:50.247
It-It's pointless arguing with you.

07:50.248 --> 07:52.716
Cool. Now, in order to pull this off,

07:52.717 --> 07:54.685
I'm gonna have to look the part.

07:54.686 --> 07:56.687
Lois, which dress may I borrow?

07:56.688 --> 07:59.755
None. My closet is off-limits.

07:59.756 --> 08:02.459
Fine. There's got to be
something in the attic.

08:02.460 --> 08:05.796
I can't even begin to describe
the density of illness

08:05.797 --> 08:07.764
I feel in my bone marrow right now.

08:07.765 --> 08:10.067
That is-that is how appalled
I am by this.

08:10.068 --> 08:11.834
- Other guys?
- Sorry, Peter.

08:11.835 --> 08:14.004
I don't see you getting away
with this one.

08:14.005 --> 08:15.671
Look, Peter, the good news is

08:15.672 --> 08:17.840
you still fit
in your wife's wedding gown.

08:17.841 --> 08:19.776
Not every guy can say that.

08:19.777 --> 08:22.179
It's actually Meg's.
She commits murders in it.

08:22.180 --> 08:23.680
What's this, now?

08:23.681 --> 08:26.182
That's just it, Peter... this
whole thing is a joke to you.

08:26.183 --> 08:28.285
Are you forgetting
I have a dad who's a woman?

08:28.286 --> 08:29.920
No, of course not.
That's the first thing

08:29.921 --> 08:31.354
everyone thinks of when they see you.

08:31.355 --> 08:32.622
But Th-this isn't like that.

08:32.623 --> 08:34.280
And I thought you guys would support me.

08:34.281 --> 08:36.840
Like we all supported Joe
on that road trip.

08:36.841 --> 08:39.997
- Boy, I am stuffed.
- Oh, I forgot to mention,

08:39.998 --> 08:42.199
one of you guys has to be in charge

08:42.200 --> 08:43.934
of changing my diaper the whole trip.

08:43.935 --> 08:45.636
Why don't we all just switch off?

08:45.637 --> 08:47.938
Oh, there will be other jobs
for other people.

08:47.939 --> 08:50.574
Okay, I guess we should,
like, draw straws or something.

08:50.575 --> 08:52.376
Actually, I've been observing all of you

08:52.377 --> 08:55.811
for the past few hours,
and I choose Quagmire.

08:55.812 --> 08:58.214
- What?! Why me?
- You've got long fingers.

08:58.215 --> 09:00.483
And I feel like you wouldn't crack

09:00.484 --> 09:02.618
if things start to go south.

09:02.619 --> 09:05.388
Fine. How do I know when it's time?

09:05.389 --> 09:07.891
Well, I'll turn to you, very sincerely,

09:07.892 --> 09:10.227
and I'll look you right in your eyes,

09:10.228 --> 09:13.896
and I'll say,
"Quagmire, I've got poopies."

09:13.897 --> 09:15.198
Ugh.

09:15.199 --> 09:16.867
Now, Quagmire, I've...

09:16.868 --> 09:18.901
- You got poopies. I know.
- No!

09:18.902 --> 09:20.938
<i>You're supposed to let me say it!</i>

09:22.739 --> 09:24.741
Quagmire...

09:24.742 --> 09:26.878
I've got poopies.

09:32.050 --> 09:33.916
- Dad!
- Dad!

09:33.917 --> 09:36.219
How goes the transition, Mr. Griffin?

09:36.220 --> 09:39.555
Like Huma Abedin, I'm trying
to forget about my Weiner.

09:39.556 --> 09:41.757
<i>Whoa, we're doing Cheers, not Frasier.</i>

09:41.758 --> 09:43.760
Tough day, Dad?

09:43.761 --> 09:45.896
I don't get it. How does Rebel Wilson

09:45.897 --> 09:47.396
always look so fetching?

09:47.397 --> 09:49.398
- Does she, though?
- You could be, too,

09:49.399 --> 09:52.003
if you just let your hair down a little.

09:55.706 --> 09:59.108
Now you just take that beautiful
hair down to the salon,

09:59.109 --> 10:00.776
and you'll be a ten.

10:00.777 --> 10:02.278
On a scale of a billion?

10:02.279 --> 10:03.546
Thanks, Chris.

10:03.547 --> 10:06.282
Thanks for helping me
at 11:30 on a school day.

10:06.283 --> 10:08.385
There was a shooting.

10:10.955 --> 10:13.223
<i>She's an old-time ambassador</i>

10:13.224 --> 10:16.094
<i>Of sweet-talking, night-walking games</i>

10:18.095 --> 10:20.229
<i>But she's a queen and such are queens</i>

10:20.230 --> 10:22.965
<i>That your laughter
is sucked in their brains.</i>

10:22.966 --> 10:25.236
I'll take 'em all.

10:28.138 --> 10:29.774
Well, hello.

10:36.147 --> 10:37.781
- Where you going, Dad?
- Out.

10:37.782 --> 10:40.891
Now that I'm living as a woman,
I can say whatever I want to men

10:40.892 --> 10:42.396
and they can't hit me.

10:44.154 --> 10:45.655
Oh, hey, Peter.

10:45.656 --> 10:47.257
Sully could've made it to an airport.

10:47.258 --> 10:49.659
Hey, you shut your mouth!
That man is a hero!

10:49.660 --> 10:51.228
Ah, ah, ah, ah! Woman.

10:51.229 --> 10:52.829
Well, it's definitely true

10:52.830 --> 10:54.930
that I respect the boundaries of women.

10:54.931 --> 10:57.334
Oh, hey, Sherry, uh,
just-just get in the fireplace.

10:57.335 --> 10:59.437
I'll-I'll spit down the chimney.

11:00.504 --> 11:02.638
Hey, Joe. How's the suspension going?

11:02.639 --> 11:04.074
When you get married,

11:04.075 --> 11:06.309
you don't think
you'll be home together all day.

11:06.310 --> 11:08.310
It's, uh... trying.

11:08.311 --> 11:10.180
Who's at the door?

11:12.016 --> 11:13.349
It's my friend!

11:13.350 --> 11:14.517
So, what's up, Peter?

11:14.518 --> 11:16.853
I just wanted to tell you
that I'm the one

11:16.854 --> 11:18.854
who planted the evidence
that got you suspended.

11:18.855 --> 11:21.391
What?! I'm gonna kill you!

11:21.392 --> 11:22.858
Ah, ah, ah! Woman.

11:22.859 --> 11:24.326
Oh, right.

11:24.327 --> 11:25.695
Joe, close the door.

11:25.696 --> 11:27.699
You're letting the bugs in.

11:29.200 --> 11:31.200
Is your daughter still killing people?

11:31.201 --> 11:32.636
She is.

11:35.739 --> 11:37.107
Hey, Chris Brown.

11:37.108 --> 11:40.142
I just wanted to say
I'm a huge fan of your music.

11:41.812 --> 11:43.814
This is just gonna make me listen more.

11:43.815 --> 11:45.515
Oh, hey, Ray Rice.

11:45.516 --> 11:47.017
Would you mind pressing "lobby"?

11:47.018 --> 11:48.951
What do you got, potatoes in your ears?

11:48.952 --> 11:50.922
I said press "lobby"!

11:54.992 --> 11:58.161
Now, Peter, one of the perks
of being a woman

11:58.162 --> 12:00.763
is that you get to go out
and have a white wine,

12:00.764 --> 12:03.333
squeak-fart lunch with your friends.

12:03.334 --> 12:05.267
Did you hear Diane's husband left her?

12:06.537 --> 12:08.238
Yeah, you could tell from the wedding

12:08.239 --> 12:10.172
they were not gonna last.

12:10.173 --> 12:12.309
Oh, it's a shame.
And they have two kids!

12:13.311 --> 12:14.677
Marriage is hard.

12:18.548 --> 12:21.917
Those machines in the ladies'
room don't vend pants, do they?

12:21.918 --> 12:24.529
Don't let 'em take my salad.
I'm still working on it.

12:27.859 --> 12:30.227
This is so great. Now that I'm a woman,

12:30.228 --> 12:33.296
I can lean-dance
into anyone's karaoke song.

12:33.297 --> 12:36.067
<i>When you were here before</i>

12:38.136 --> 12:41.438
<i>Couldn't look you in the eye...</i>

12:41.439 --> 12:43.440
Yeah! It's a work night!

12:43.441 --> 12:45.041
Hey, come on.

12:45.042 --> 12:46.209
Get out of here.

12:46.210 --> 12:48.310
You're ruining my birthday party.

12:48.311 --> 12:51.080
<i>Your skin makes me cry...</i>

12:51.081 --> 12:53.083
Sing Justin Timberlake!

12:53.084 --> 12:55.719
Come on! I waited an hour
and a half for this!

12:55.720 --> 12:58.320
And, hey, get off that bar!

12:58.321 --> 12:59.589
Why?

12:59.590 --> 13:01.992
Because you're at Lowfan O'Reilly's.

13:04.561 --> 13:06.262
All right, where am I on the screen?

13:06.263 --> 13:08.230
Oh. "Float like a feather
in a beautiful world."

13:08.231 --> 13:09.598
Dah, dah, dah. Okay.

13:09.599 --> 13:12.571
<i>Flippin' special</i>

13:14.037 --> 13:17.676
<i>But I'm a creep...</i>

13:22.228 --> 13:24.574
What? What happened?

13:24.575 --> 13:26.182
Ah, I knew you'd catch it.

13:26.183 --> 13:28.400
I'm parting my hair
on the other side now.

13:28.401 --> 13:30.954
Oh, Peter, thank God you're okay.

13:30.955 --> 13:33.089
Hello, bosses and not my family.

13:33.090 --> 13:35.257
You really gave us a scare there.

13:35.258 --> 13:36.459
Oh, what do you mean?

13:36.460 --> 13:37.694
Well, you went into a coma

13:37.695 --> 13:39.762
after you were hit in the head by a fan.

13:39.763 --> 13:41.198
Oh, it was funny.

13:41.199 --> 13:43.465
- And then it wasn't.
- A coma?

13:43.466 --> 13:46.275
Well, I feel tomato now, beige spots.

13:46.276 --> 13:49.638
And since the company was paying
for your medical care anyway,

13:49.639 --> 13:52.508
we fulfilled your letter
of medical intent

13:52.509 --> 13:54.810
for your sex reassignment surgery.

13:54.811 --> 13:56.813
- What?
- She's saying that your surgery

13:56.814 --> 13:59.114
to become a woman
was a complete success.

13:59.115 --> 14:01.184
It's much easier going that way,
believe me.

14:01.185 --> 14:02.786
Just a chop and a mop.

14:02.787 --> 14:04.119
Congratulations, Peter.

14:04.120 --> 14:06.486
You're officially a woman.

14:09.960 --> 14:13.164
No...!

14:14.165 --> 14:17.169
That is one nutty hospital.

14:22.373 --> 14:25.374
Peter, I'm sorry this happened,
but it's your own fault.

14:25.375 --> 14:27.810
You should never have pretended
to be someone else.

14:27.811 --> 14:29.478
That's right, but now that it's done,

14:29.479 --> 14:31.348
maybe I can help you
with the transition.

14:31.349 --> 14:33.983
You know, I've always been a
great supporter of the LGBLT...

14:33.984 --> 14:35.218
- Nope.
- LGTE.

14:35.219 --> 14:36.386
- No.
- GED.

14:36.387 --> 14:37.720
- Unrelated.
- L.I.E.

14:37.721 --> 14:39.989
- The Long Island Expressway?
- NKOTB?

14:39.990 --> 14:42.057
- The wrong stuff, Brian.
- WNBA?

14:42.058 --> 14:45.161
Yes. Yes, WNBA.

14:45.162 --> 14:47.363
Mom, you know, our world today is filled

14:47.364 --> 14:49.833
with people like Dad trying
to find their identities.

14:49.834 --> 14:52.502
Whether it's cutters,
or people who cut themselves,

14:52.503 --> 14:56.171
or people who drag knives across
their thighs to feel something.

14:56.172 --> 14:57.540
You're right, Meg.

14:57.541 --> 14:59.743
I guess we'll just have
to deal with this,

14:59.744 --> 15:01.744
like when Chris won
that hundred-dollar scratcher

15:01.745 --> 15:03.847
and talked down to everybody.

15:03.848 --> 15:05.848
Your house is so cozy, Joe.

15:05.849 --> 15:08.184
Wish I could get by
with just two bathrooms.

15:08.185 --> 15:09.752
Technically, one and a half.

15:09.753 --> 15:11.655
Leave us alone.

15:11.656 --> 15:14.023
<i>I said, "Leave us alone," but deep down,</i>

15:14.024 --> 15:17.260
<i>I respected and even desired
Chris for his success.</i>

15:17.261 --> 15:19.262
<i>It would take another eight years</i>

15:19.263 --> 15:20.763
<i>before I summoned the courage</i>

15:20.764 --> 15:22.732
<i>to kiss him at a backyard barbecue,</i>

15:22.733 --> 15:24.467
<i>and from that moment on...</i>

15:24.468 --> 15:26.271
Bonnie! Bonnie!

15:27.078 --> 15:29.124
I've got poopies.

15:33.878 --> 15:35.945
Thank you for showing me the 90 things

15:35.946 --> 15:37.914
women have to do before going to bed.

15:37.915 --> 15:40.949
Okay, now quick break
to cry for no reason.

15:40.950 --> 15:44.387
Can we do one last judgmental
scroll through Facebook first?

15:44.388 --> 15:45.916
Of course.

15:46.389 --> 15:48.958
Congratulations,
you went to a dance club.

15:48.959 --> 15:51.026
You know, Peter,
if I didn't know better,

15:51.027 --> 15:52.829
I'd say you'd been a woman for years.

15:52.830 --> 15:54.863
Now we just drift off to sleep,

15:54.864 --> 15:56.733
thinking about Rick from Midas Muffler.

15:56.734 --> 15:58.435
I probably won't be able to sleep

15:58.436 --> 16:01.304
'cause I had two sips of tea
at 3:30 this afternoon.

16:01.305 --> 16:02.738
That's okay, Peter.

16:02.739 --> 16:05.307
You can just read
on an impossibly bright iPad

16:05.308 --> 16:07.845
while I toss and turn in a pissy way.

16:15.485 --> 16:17.753
You almost done with the chapter?

16:17.754 --> 16:20.305
Oh, there's no chapters.
It's a Clifford book.

16:24.936 --> 16:26.905
Thank you, young man.

16:27.923 --> 16:29.431
Hey, now that we're all settled
at this table,

16:29.432 --> 16:32.201
you guys want to move outside
'cause it's such a nice day?

16:32.202 --> 16:34.304
Okay, why don't you go save us
a table outside,

16:34.305 --> 16:35.704
and we'll be there soon?

16:37.108 --> 16:38.882
Taken. Sorry.

16:42.105 --> 16:43.345
You know, it's fun back here.

16:43.346 --> 16:45.348
You don't even know you're in Quahog.

16:45.349 --> 16:47.584
Please don't talk to us. You're too fat.

16:49.286 --> 16:51.621
You want me to start a new tab for you?

16:51.622 --> 16:53.288
No, you can just keep ours going.

16:53.289 --> 16:55.357
Your friends left
the minute you came out here,

16:55.358 --> 16:57.594
and they didn't pay their indoor tab.

16:58.796 --> 17:00.796
I feel so alone.

17:00.797 --> 17:03.468
And that bitch stole my hairstyles!

17:04.501 --> 17:06.369
Well, hello.

17:06.370 --> 17:08.638
That's what he said to me!

17:17.480 --> 17:18.648
Peter?

17:18.649 --> 17:21.617
- Ida?
- Come, sit.

17:21.618 --> 17:23.353
Well, look at you.

17:23.354 --> 17:25.354
Yeah, look at me.

17:25.355 --> 17:27.757
- What's wrong?
- It's a long story.

17:27.758 --> 17:29.491
Yeah, I've heard.

17:29.492 --> 17:32.094
Peter, everything is gonna be okay.

17:32.095 --> 17:33.496
I promise.

17:33.497 --> 17:34.930
O-Okay.

17:34.931 --> 17:37.199
Now, I'm going to tell you a story.

17:37.200 --> 17:39.102
When I first met you, Peter,

17:39.103 --> 17:41.738
I was already at the end
of a long journey

17:41.739 --> 17:43.706
to find the courage to become a woman.

17:43.707 --> 17:46.843
But before that, I lived for 61 years

17:46.844 --> 17:49.778
as a miserable, miserable man.

17:49.779 --> 17:52.582
I grew up in the small town
of Football, Texas,

17:52.583 --> 17:55.617
and from the age of eight,
I was mercilessly teased

17:55.618 --> 17:59.255
for being different
and "dressing funny."

17:59.256 --> 18:02.392
Then, at the age of 14,
I had an epiphany.

18:02.393 --> 18:03.992
It was so clear.

18:03.993 --> 18:07.330
I was a girl trapped in a boy's body.

18:07.331 --> 18:10.333
I'm having a hard time focusing
without a drink, but go on.

18:10.334 --> 18:15.270
It took me 47 years from that
day to officially own who I am.

18:15.271 --> 18:17.207
Is there a waiter or...?

18:17.208 --> 18:21.210
In those 47 years, I became
an expert at hiding my secret.

18:21.211 --> 18:24.080
I became a war hero and raised a family,

18:24.081 --> 18:27.851
but I was dying inside,
and the deeper I buried it,

18:27.852 --> 18:29.952
the more unhappy I became,

18:29.953 --> 18:32.921
and eventually, I even thought
of ending my own life.

18:32.922 --> 18:35.424
But I couldn't do that to Glenn.

18:35.425 --> 18:37.392
I had no idea.

18:37.393 --> 18:39.394
It's clear you had no idea.

18:39.395 --> 18:41.397
You know nothing about what it means

18:41.398 --> 18:42.599
to feel this struggle.

18:42.600 --> 18:44.534
Yeah, you're right.

18:44.535 --> 18:46.635
I kind of stumbled into all this,

18:46.636 --> 18:49.272
but you've been dealing with it
your whole life.

18:49.273 --> 18:51.039
Yes, I have.

18:51.040 --> 18:53.676
And my story, to one degree or another,

18:53.677 --> 18:56.078
is every transgender person's story,

18:56.079 --> 18:58.747
and all those stories
are the price of admission

18:58.748 --> 19:01.750
to finally feeling at peace
with who you are...

19:01.751 --> 19:03.920
A price you never paid.

19:03.921 --> 19:06.256
Ah, I'm so sorry, Ida.

19:06.257 --> 19:07.757
I feel really awful,

19:07.758 --> 19:11.094
and I'm a really bad person
for what I did.

19:11.095 --> 19:12.981
I deserve what happened to me.

19:13.963 --> 19:15.965
Touching story, other people humans.

19:15.966 --> 19:17.866
Now, could you direct me

19:17.867 --> 19:20.769
to Earth's reserve of other dog butts?

19:20.770 --> 19:22.772
That's right, that's right.

19:22.773 --> 19:25.307
Everybody natural.

19:25.308 --> 19:26.942
Peter, listen to me.

19:26.943 --> 19:28.777
<i>You were a bad person.</i>

19:28.778 --> 19:30.947
But now you've taken a journey.

19:30.948 --> 19:34.116
It just took becoming a woman
to make you a better man.

19:34.117 --> 19:36.119
But I'll never be that better man.

19:36.120 --> 19:38.086
I can't afford the surgery to go back.

19:38.087 --> 19:40.989
I think I might be able
to help you with that, Peter.

19:40.990 --> 19:42.624
- Really?
- Yes.

19:42.625 --> 19:44.628
I've got an idea.

19:47.224 --> 19:49.500
What a day.

19:53.504 --> 19:55.438
Oh, Peter, you started a Kickstarter.

19:55.439 --> 19:57.140
Not exactly.

19:57.141 --> 20:00.142
Oh, that's... that's not a "K."

20:00.143 --> 20:02.010
Look at that. You're up to six inches.

20:02.011 --> 20:03.645
That's two inches past your goal.

20:03.646 --> 20:05.448
It's not important what the goal was.

20:05.449 --> 20:08.985
What's important is
this community cares.

20:08.986 --> 20:10.319
Congratulations, Mr. Griffin.

20:10.320 --> 20:12.154
Your surgery was a success.

20:12.155 --> 20:13.457
You're a man again.

20:14.343 --> 20:15.946
Sully was a hero!

20:21.398 --> 20:23.666
Well, I'm glad
everything's back to normal.

20:23.667 --> 20:25.000
I'll say.

20:25.001 --> 20:27.703
Dad, you lost a wiener
but came out a winner.

20:29.006 --> 20:31.106
Well, that does it
for our crossover episode.

20:31.107 --> 20:33.343
<i>Thanks for coming,
cast of Bob's Burgers.</i>

20:33.344 --> 20:35.244
We didn't get to do anything.

20:35.245 --> 20:36.478
Show's 22 minutes long.

20:36.479 --> 20:37.880
Not everything makes it to air.

20:37.881 --> 20:39.315
But, hey, you have the floor

20:39.316 --> 20:40.865
if there's something hilarious
you want to say.

20:40.866 --> 20:42.493
I'll just sit here and be quiet.

20:42.494 --> 20:44.853
Give us two Emmys worth of amazing.

20:44.854 --> 20:47.422
Maybe a funny burger name? No?

20:47.423 --> 20:49.359
Girl in the bunny ears?

20:49.360 --> 20:51.827
Boy, I love it when characters
are expressed by props.

20:51.828 --> 20:54.430
I kind of feel like
this is less of a crossover

20:54.431 --> 20:55.832
and more of a roast.

20:55.833 --> 20:57.869
No, a roast is good-natured.

20:57.870 --> 20:59.870
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv